@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@ ProfiCare PC-PW 3008 BT = Same Chipsea "WeChat scale" firmware as the Hoffen BBS
 HuaweiHagridWspHandler = The scale only answers after a Huawei Hagrid handshake, so CAK, C1 and C2 (32 hex characters each) have to be entered in the device settings first
 AiLink Body Fat Scale = Non-connectable: the whole measurement is TEA-encrypted inside the advertisement, so no pairing is needed and the vendor "AiLink" app can be removed. Covers the AiLink/eLink broadcast family (advertises service 0xF0A0, often named "EL1")
 PICOOC Mini Lite = Tested with the PICOOC-L broadcast protocol. Weight and impedance are recorded, and the adult Caucasian/White body-composition path is a clean-room port of the PICOOC 4.3.0 ARM64 implementation.
+PICOOC-CQ = Includes Mini Pro (13-byte measurement frames) and S3 Lite V2.0 (16-byte frames). Weight and impedance are recorded; missing body-composition values are estimated by openScale's StandardImpedanceLib.
 QN Scale (Broadcast) = No pairing needed. Tested with the FITINDEX FT-26R-W, which reports weight only (no body composition — these units have no electrodes). Stay on the scale until the display stops changing, around six seconds; it only reports a reading once it settles, so stepping off earlier records nothing.
 AAAxHandler = No pairing needed: the Icomon/Fitdays "AAA" boards only broadcast. Weight only; the impedance frame is not decoded. Newer boards (e.g. "AAA07A", Posture FG220LB) are recognised by their advertisement, not just by name.
 Fitdays FG2202WB = Body composition needs the handlebar held during the weigh-in; with feet only the scale measures no impedance
